<title>GERMANY: BUBA council member sees wider equities interest.</title>
<headline>BUBA council member sees wider equities interest.</headline>
<dateline>MUNICH 1997-07-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bundesbank council member Franz-Christoph Zeitler said on Friday he hoped that the &quot;quantum leap&quot; in German investors' interest in stock market investment would survive inevitable share price declines.</p>
<p>Zeitler said in the text of a speech that the privatisation last year of Deutsche Telekom AG had helped give a boost to the German equity market culture.</p>
<p>&quot;Interest in the share market has made a quantum leap forward, not least due to the Telekom privatisation, and one can only hope that it will survive inevitable setbacks in stock market prices,&quot; Zeitler said in a speech prepared for delivery at a conference in Munich.</p>
<p>Germany's DAX index of 30 leading stocks has jumped about 45 percent this year.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
